@*
    Why this row is going where it is going.

    A destination reads like any other once it has been rendered. "Dungeon
    Blocks/Unsorted/UD 067 Hole Trap" and "Dungeon Blocks/The Ultimate
    Dungeon/UD 067 Hole Trap" are the same shape, and nothing on the page said
    which token produced which segment -- so a pack that split where it was not
    expected to, or a mini filed under the wrong designer, could only be
    explained by opening the model and guessing backwards.

    Shown as the template's own tokens rather than as prose. The person reading
    this wrote the template; naming its parts back to them is the shortest route
    from "that is wrong" to knowing which field to change.

    A token with nothing behind it is called out rather than shown as its
    placeholder, because "Unsorted" the answer and "Unsorted" the designer's
    name are indistinguishable written down, and telling them apart is the
    reason to look.
*@

@* Which cuts of the mini are travelling. Two folders holding one sculpt plan
   two moves whose destinations differ only in a level that says nothing about
   which is which -- so "otto bismark" and "otto bismark" read identically here,
   and the only clue was whether the folder being left happened to be named
   after its contents. A variant combination is what makes one copy distinct,
   so it is stated rather than inferred. *@
@if (Variants.Count > 0)
{
    <div class="token-trace mt-1">
        <span class="token-part">
            <span class="token-name">carrying</span>
            <span class="token-value">@string.Join(", ", Variants)</span>
        </span>
    </div>
}

@if (Tokens.Count > 0)
{
    <div class="token-trace mt-1">
        @foreach (var token in Tokens)
        {
            <span class="token-part">
                <span class="token-name">@token.Name</span>
                @if (token.Value is { } value)
                {
                    <span class="token-value">@value</span>
                }
                else
                {
                    <span class="token-empty">nothing &mdash; placeholder used</span>
                }
            </span>
        }
    </div>
}

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public IReadOnlyList<ResolvedToken> Tokens { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The variants the meshes in this row carry.</summary>
    [Parameter] public IReadOnlyList<string> Variants { get; set; } = [];
}
